<title>UK: GOLF-LEADING WORLD RANKINGS.</title>
<headline>GOLF-LEADING WORLD RANKINGS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Tom Lehman replaced</p>
<p>Australian Greg Norman at the top of the world golf rankings</p>
<p>list issued on Monday.</p>
<p>Norman had topped the rankings for a record 96 weeks.</p>
<p>Lehman, who finished joint fourth in the MCI classic won by</p>
<p>Zimbabwe's Nick Price in South Carolina at the weekend, became</p>
<p>only the eighth player to hold the number one position since the</p>
<p>rankings were introduced 11 years ago.</p>
<p>Top 20 (U.S. unless stated)</p>
<p>  1. Tom Lehman			    9.90 points average</p>
<p>  2. Greg Norman (Australia)	   9.80</p>
<p>  3. Steve Elkington (Australia)     8.79</p>
<p>  4. Nick Price (Zimbabwe)	     8.76</p>
<p>  5. Tiger Woods			   8.73</p>
<p>  6. Colin Montgomerie (Britain)     8.68</p>
<p>  7. Mark O'Meara			  8.43</p>
<p>  8. Ernie Els (South Africa)	  8.41</p>
<p>  9. Masashi Ozaki (Japan)	     8.30</p>
<p> 10. Phil Mickelson			7.27</p>
<p> 11. Fred Couples			  7.00</p>
<p> 12. Nick Faldo (Britain)		6.64</p>
<p> 13. Scott Hoch			    6.48</p>
<p> 14. Brad Faxon			    6.10</p>
<p> 15. Davis Love			    5.92</p>
<p> 15. Steve Jones			   5.74</p>
<p> 16. Jesper Parnevik (Sweden)	  5.79</p>
<p> 17. Steve Jones			   5.74</p>
<p> 18. Corey Pavin			   5.68</p>
<p> 19. Tom Watson			    5.60</p>
<p> 20. Bernhard Langer (Germany)	 5.53</p>
